  "issue_title": "Reconstruct mutable GitHub fields from event history",
  "issue_body": "**Context**\nThis PR correctly drops labels, repository label lists, and milestone due dates from frozen GitHub context because the current REST snapshots are mutable and can leak post-freeze information. If these fields are useful to future benchmark tasks, they should return only through an event/timeline-based reconstruction path that can prove the value as of T.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] Reconstruct issue and PR labels as of `_knowable_until` from timeline/events data.\n- [ ] Reconstruct repository label availability as of `_knowable_until`, or explicitly document why it remains unsupported.\n- [ ] Reconstruct milestone due dates only if historical edits can be recovered; otherwise keep them omitted.\n- [ ] Add regression tests showing post-T label and milestone mutations do not appear in frozen context.\n\n**Pointers**: `benchmark/github_context.py`, `fetch_context_at`, `_issue_record`, `_milestone_at`, `tests/test_github_context.py`",
